the lead cut to a point or two would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tony Evers (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Wisconsin's governorship is open as two-term Democrat Tony Evers retires, setting up a contest between Milwaukee County Executive David Crowley and Republican Tom Tiffany in a state that has split nearly evenly in recent elections. Every likely-voter poll since midsummer has shown Crowley ahead by three to five points, though the most recent surveys date to late August. Rating outlets lean Democratic, several call it a tossup, and prediction markets put Crowley's odds near four in five.\n\nThe clearest structural advantage belongs to Tiffany financially: he has raised roughly ten times as much as Crowley and enters the fall with about $3 million on hand. Late-September coverage has centered on affordability, energy policy, and questions about Tiffany's transparency and a driving incident. Current evidence points to a close race tilting Democratic.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7127, "margin": 2.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7543, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7549, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7725, "margin": 3.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7589, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7208, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.724, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7645, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7536, "margin": 3.5}]}